Tracked so this directory exists in a fresh checkout.

scripts/security-scan writes Trivy's JSON reports here, and
backend/tests/test_trivy.py asserts the directory exists — that is a
structural check on the repo, not on whether a scan has been run. The
reports themselves stay ignored; see .gitignore.

Without this the directory only existed on machines where somebody had
already run a scan, so those two tests passed locally and failed the
first time CI ever ran them.
